---
import { agentList } from "../agents.ts"
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"
import "../styles/home.css"
---

<Base
  title="What you can do with olai"
  description="Give a task to an AI agent, see what is due, and capture a thought. Each picture shows the real app."
>
<main>

<div class="pagehead">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">uses</p>
    <h1>What you can do with olai</h1>
    <p>olai holds Markdown documents and outlines. This page shows four things
    that you can do with them. Each picture shows the real app.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<section id="notes">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Keep Markdown notes</h2>
    <div class="use flip">
      <div>
        <p>olai opens a directory of Markdown files as it is. Each document
        has a page, with its headings, its properties, and a list of what
        links to it.</p>
        <p>A standard Markdown link opens another document, a heading, or an
        item of an outline. Search reads the text of every document.</p>
        <p>You can start a chat with an agent about one document. The agent
        reads the document, and changes it when you ask.</p>
        <p class="needs">Wikilinks are upcoming. Today olai shows <code>[[page]]</code> as text. Read <a href="/#upcoming">what is upcoming for Markdown</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <div class="shot small"><img src="/tour/document.png" width="2880" height="1800" alt="A Markdown document in olai, with two headings, a table, a task list, and the item that links to the document."></div>
        <figcaption class="caption">The real app. A document, with a table, a task list, and the item that links to it.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="give">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Give a task to an agent</h2>
    <div class="use">
      <div>
        <p>A project is an outline. You do some items yourself, and you give
        other items to an agent.</p>
        <p>A chat belongs to one item or to one document. Next week the chat is
        still there, with everything that the agent did.</p>
        <p>You can start agents on several items. Each item shows what its agent
        is doing, and the sidebar lists the agents that wait for an answer.
        Eight agents can run at the same time.</p>
        <p class="needs">An agent needs an account with {agentList}. Read <a href="/docs/giving-an-agent-work/">how to give an agent work</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <div class="shot small"><img src="/tour/outline-and-chat.png" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" alt="An outline beside a chat. In the chat an agent has marked items of the outline done."></div>
        <figcaption class="caption">The real app. The agent in this picture is scripted.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="due">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>See what is due</h2>
    <div class="use flip">
      <div>
        <p>An item can have a date. The <strong>Agenda</strong> page lists the
        dated items from every outline. Late items are first, then the items for
        today, then the items for later days.</p>
        <p>Each day has a page of its own. The page shows the items that have
        that date.</p>
        <p>An item that repeats comes back as a new item on its next date.</p>
        <p class="needs">Read about <a href="/docs/dates-and-status/">marks, days, and repeating</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <div class="shot small"><img src="/tour/agenda.png" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" alt="The Agenda page, with one late item at the top."></div>
        <figcaption class="caption">The real app. One item is late, one is due today, and two are due on later days.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="capture">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Capture a thought</h2>
    <div class="use">
      <div>
        <p>The palette has a command named <strong>Capture to the
        Inbox</strong>. The item that you type there goes to the inbox, with
        the date of today and the mark <strong>To do</strong>. You move the
        item to an outline later.</p>
        <p>The command also works in a phone browser, if the phone can reach
        your computer. A terminal command does the same.</p>
        <p class="needs">Read about <a href="/docs/getting-around/">the sidebar, tabs, and the palette</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <div class="shot small"><img src="/tour/capture.png" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" alt="The palette, open over an outline, with the command Capture to the Inbox selected."></div>
        <figcaption class="caption">The real app. The palette, after you type "capture".</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Check what olai needs before you start</h2>
    <p class="lead">olai is new. It runs on a Mac or a Linux computer, and you
    start it from a terminal. Read
    <a href="/#try">what you need to run olai</a>. Or read
    <a href="/#compare">how olai compares with Obsidian, Logseq, Roam Research, and Workflowy</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

</main>
</Base>
